WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.596
The results are consistent and strong.

00:00:02.676 --> 00:00:04.357
On in-domain forecasting,

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:10.907
TimeSiam cuts average mean squared error by five
point seven percent with a PatchTST backbone

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:14.077
and two point five percent with iTransformer,

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:18.936
and remember these backbones already forecast very
well from scratch.

00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:20.908
On in-domain classification,

00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:26.684
it lifts average accuracy by eleven point five
percent over random initialization.

00:00:26.764 --> 00:00:32.318
Across all these settings TimeSiam beats eight
strong self-supervised baselines.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:38.587
Perhaps the most striking finding is in
cross-domain transfer: pre-training on the large,

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:45.207
diverse TSLD-1G dataset and fine-tuning elsewhere
sometimes beats even in-domain pre-training,

00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:50.560
which confirms that scale and diversity of
pre-training data really pay off.
